[{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>The function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfies <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=e^{-x^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(2)=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. For each of the following, use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_{n+1}=y_n+h f(x_n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to approximate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with the given value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer to three decimal places:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.25\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =2,\\quad y_0=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =1+0.5f(2)=1+0.5\\times0.0183156889\\ldots=1.009157819\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =2+0.5=2.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_1+0.5f(x_1)=1.009157819\\ldots+0.5\\times0.001930454136\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1.01012304\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =2.5+0.5=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y =1.010\\text{ (3 DP)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =2,\\quad y_0=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =1+0.25f(2)=1+0.25\\times0.018315688\\ldots=1.00457890972\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =2+0.25=2.25\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_1+0.25f(x_1)=1.00457890972\\ldots+0.25\\times0.00632971542749\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1.006161613\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =2.25+0.25=2.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_3 =y_2+0.25f(x_2)=1.006161613\\ldots+0.25\\times0.001930454\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1.00664395211\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_3 =2.5+0.25=2.75\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_4 =y_3+0.25f(x_3)=1.00664395211\\ldots+0.25\\times0.00051957\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1.00677384578\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_4 =2.75+0.25=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y =1.007\\text{ (3 DP)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>The function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfies <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=x^2-y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(0)=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. For each of the following, use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_{n+1}=y_n+h f(x_n,y_n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to approximate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(0.4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with the given value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer to three decimal places:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =0,\\quad y_0=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =y_0+hf(x_0,y_0)=1+0.2f(0,1)=1+0.2\\times(-1)=0.8\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =0+0.2=0.2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_1+hf(x_1,y_1)=0.8+0.2f(0.2,0.8)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =0.8+0.2\\times(-0.76)=0.648\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =0.2+0.2=0.4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y =0.648\\text{ (3 DP)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =0,\\quad y_0=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =y_0+hf(x_0,y_0)=1+hf(0,1)=1+0.1\\times(-1)=0.9\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =0+0.1=0.1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_1+hf(x_1,y_1)=0.9+0.1f(0.1,0.9)=0.9+0.1\\times(-0.89)=0.811\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =0.1+0.1=0.2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_3 =y_2+hf(x_2,y_2)=0.811+0.1f(0.2,0.811)=0.811+0.1\\times(-0.771)=0.7339\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_3 =0.2+0.1=0.3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_4 =y_3+hf(x_3,y_3)=0.7339+0.1f(0.3,0.7339)=0.7339+0.1\\times(-0.6439)=0.66951\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_4 =0.3+0.1=0.4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y =0.670\\text{ (3 DP)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>The function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfies <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\sin x-y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(0)=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Calculate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(0.4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> using Euler's step by step method for the given value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer to three decimal places:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =0,\\quad y_0=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =y_0+hf(x_0,y_0)=2+0.2f(0,2)=2+0.2\\times(-2)=1.6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =0+0.2=0.2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_1+hf(x_1,y_1)=1.6+0.2f(0.2,1.6)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1.6+0.2\\times(-1.4013306692\\ldots)=1.3197338662\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =0.2+0.2=0.4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y =1.320\\text{ (3 DP)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =0,\\quad y_0=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =2+0.1f(0,2)=2+0.1\\times(-2)=1.8\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =0+0.1=0.1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =1.8+0.1f(0.1,1.8)=1.8+0.1\\times(-1.7001665834\\ldots)=1.6299833417\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =0.1+0.1=0.2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_3 =1.6299833417\\ldots+0.1f(0.2,1.6299833417\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1.6299833417\\ldots+0.1\\times(-1.4313140109\\ldots)=1.486851941\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_3 =0.2+0.1=0.3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_4 =1.486851941\\ldots+0.1f(0.3,1.486851941\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1.486851941\\ldots+0.1\\times(-1.1913317339)=1.3677187672\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_4 =0.3+0.1=0.4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y =1.368\\text{ (3 DP)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>The function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfies the differential equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{x^2+y}{y^2-x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the condition <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(2)=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Use two iterations of Euler's step by step method to estimate the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =2,\\quad y_0=-1,\\quad h=0.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =y_0+hf(x_0,y_0)=-1+0.5f(2,-1)=-1+0.5\\times(-3)=-2.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =2+0.5=2.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_1+hf(x_1,y_1)=-2.5+0.5f(2.5,-2.5)=-2.5+0.5\\times1=-2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =2.5+0.5=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y =-2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>For each of the following, use Euler's step by step method:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=e^{\\sqrt{x}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Estimate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer to three decimal places.</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\ln(x^2+y)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Estimate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(1.5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer to three decimal places.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx} =\\frac{e^{\\sqrt{x}}}{2x},\\quad x_0=4,\\quad y_0=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =y_0+hf(x_0)=1+0.5f(4)=1+0.5\\times0.9236320124\\ldots=1.46186006\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =4+0.5=4.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_1+hf(x_1)=1.46186006\\ldots+0.5f(4.5)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1.46186006\\ldots+0.5\\times0.9269049685\\ldots=1.92526849\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =4.5+0.5=5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y =1.925\\text{ (3 DP)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =0,\\quad y_0=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =2+0.5f(0,2)=2+0.5\\times0.3465735903\\ldots=2.1732867951\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =0+0.5=0.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_1+0.5f(x_1,y_1)=2.1732867951\\ldots+0.5f(0.5,2.1732867951\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =2.1732867951\\ldots+0.5\\times0.4072747327\\ldots=2.3769241615\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =0.5+0.5=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_3 =y_2+0.5f(1,y_2)=2.3769241615\\ldots+0.5f(1,2.3769241615\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =2.3769241615\\ldots+0.5\\times0.5119916334\\ldots=2.6329199781\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_3 =1+0.5=1.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y =2.633\\text{ (3 DP)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>The function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfies <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=2e^{2x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the condition <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(0)=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Use Euler's step by step method with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to approximate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(0.6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer to three decimal places.</p></li><li><p>Find the exact value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(0.6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the relative error.</p></li><li><p>State whether the Euler approximation to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(0.6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an over- or an under-estimate of the exact value, giving a reason for your answer.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =0,\\quad y_0=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =y_0+hf(x_0)=1+0.2f(0)=1+0.2\\times2=1.4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =0+0.2=0.2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_1+hf(x_1)=1.4+0.2f(0.2)=1.4+0.2\\times2e^{0.4}\\ldots=1.996729879\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =0.2+0.2=0.4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_3 =y_2+hf(x_2)=1.996729879\\ldots+0.2f(0.4)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1.996729879\\ldots+0.2\\times2e^{0.8}\\ldots=2.88694625\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_3 =0.4+0.2=0.6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y =2.887\\text{ (3 DP)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Separating and integrating gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^{2x}+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(0)=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1=e^0+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^{2x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0.6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^{1.2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>The relative error is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{2.887-e^{1.2}}{e^{1.2}}=-0.130.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>The relative error is negative, which means the approximate value is less than the exact value. Therefore, the Euler approximation underestimates the true value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(0.6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>The function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfies <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=x+3\\cos y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the condition <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(1)=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Use Euler's step by step method with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to approximate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(2.2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer to three decimal places.</p></li><li><p>Comment on the reliability of your result.</p></li><li><p>Explain how you could use this formula to find an improved approximation to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(2.2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =1,\\quad y_0=4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =y_0+hf(x_0,y_0)=4+0.4f(1,4)=4+0.4\\times(-0.9609308626\\ldots)=3.6156276550\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =1+0.4=1.4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_1+hf(x_1,y_1)=3.6156276550\\ldots+0.4f(1.4,3.6156276550\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =3.6156276550\\ldots+0.4\\times(-1.2692009154\\ldots)=3.1079472888\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =1.4+0.4=1.8\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_3 =y_2+hf(x_2,y_2)=3.1079472888\\ldots+0.4f(1.8,3.1079472888\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =3.1079472888\\ldots+0.4\\times(-1.1983021443\\ldots)=2.6286264311\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_3 =1.8+0.4=2.2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y =2.629\\text{ (3 DP)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Not very reliable as Euler's step by step method assumes the gradient is constant over each step, which is not true here since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> changes rapidly.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Increase the number of steps (use a smaller value for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span>).</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>A drug concentration <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> mg depends on how much is already in the bloodstream and the time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hours since infusion started. It may be modelled by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dC}{dt}=5-0.2C+0.1t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Initially there is no drug in the bloodstream. Use Euler's method with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hours to estimate the concentration after 1 hour.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_0 =0,\\quad C_0=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C_1 =C_0+hf(t_0,C_0)=0+0.5f(0,0)=0+0.5\\times5=2.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_1 =0+0.5=0.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C_2 =C_1+hf(t_1,C_1)=2.5+0.5f(0.5,2.5)=2.5+0.5\\times4.55=4.775\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_2 =0.5+0.5=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore C \\approx4.775\\text{ mg}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>A town's population <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of people grows depending on the current population and the season. It may be modelled by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=0.005y+200\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}x\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of months passed and is measured in radians. Initially the population is 12,000 people. Use Euler's method with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> month to approximate the population after 3 months.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =0,\\quad y_0=12000\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =y_0+hf(x_0,y_0)=12000+f(0,12000)=12060\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =0+1=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_1+hf(x_1,y_1)=12060+f(1,12060)=12220.3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =1+1=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_3 =y_2+hf(x_2,y_2)=12220.3+f(2,12220.3)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =12220.3+234.3065808\\ldots=12454.6065808\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_3 =2+1=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y =12455\\text{ people}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>The temperature of a rod <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T^\\circ\\mathrm C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> over time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> minutes may be modelled by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dT}{dt}=0.2t-0.05T\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. When 5 minutes have passed, the rod is at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"50^\\circ\\mathrm C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Use Euler's method with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> minute to estimate the temperature after 8 minutes, giving your answer to three significant figures.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_0 =5,\\quad T_0=50\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"T_1 =T_0+hf(t_0,T_0)=50+1f(5,50)=50+5\\times(-1.5)=48.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_1 =5+1=6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"T_2 =T_1+hf(t_1,T_1)=48.5+1f(6,48.5)=48.5+1\\times(-1.225)=47.275\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_2 =6+1=7\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"T_3 =T_2+hf(t_2,T_2)=47.275+1f(7,47.275)=47.275+1\\times(-0.963750)=46.31125\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_3 =7+1=8\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore T =46.3^\\circ\\mathrm C\\text{ (3 SF)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>The balance <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pounds B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on an account grows depending on both balance and a time-varying interest rate, and may be modelled by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dB}{dt}=0.01B+5\\cos(0.5t)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> months have passed. The account is checked after 2 months and the balance is £970. Use Euler's method twice to estimate the balance after a further 2 months. <strong>Prerequisite Knowledge for Q12: Integration of Standard Functions</strong></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_0 =2,\\quad B_0=970,\\quad h=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"B_1 =B_0+hf(t_0,B_0)=970+1f(2,970)=970+12.401511529\\ldots=982.401511529\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_1 =2+1=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"B_2 =y_1+hf(t_1,B_1)=982.401511529\\ldots+1f(3,982.401511529\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =12.401511529\\ldots+10.177701124\\ldots=992.579212653\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_2 =3+1=4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore B =\\pounds992.58\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>The function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> passes through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and satisfies the differential equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Use three iterations of Euler's step by step method to estimate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(0.3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer to three decimal places.</p></li><li><p>Explain why this method underestimates the true value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(0.3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =0,\\quad y_0=1,\\quad h=0.1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =y_0+hf(x_0)=1+0.1f(0)=1+0.1\\times0=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =0+0.1=0.1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_1+hf(x_1)=1+0.1f(0.1)=1+0.1\\times0.0998334167\\ldots=1.009983342\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =0.1+0.1=0.2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_3 =y_2+hf(x_2)=1.009983342\\ldots+0.1f(0.2)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1.009983342\\ldots+0.1\\times0.1986693308\\ldots=1.029850275\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_3 =0.2+0.1=0.3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y =1.030\\text{ (3 DP)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\cos x+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is concave, so the tangents lie below the curve, so each step gives a value that is slightly too small, so it is an under-estimate. Alternatively, integrating gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\cos x+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1=-\\cos0+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\cos x+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0.3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\cos0.3+2=1.044664\\ldots&gt;1.30\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so this is an under-estimate.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>A curve satisfies <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{2x-y}{xy}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,a)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a&gt;2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Using Euler's step by step method, with starting point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,a)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, gives an estimate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=4.450\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =3,\\quad y_0=a\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =y_0+hf(x_0,y_0)=a+0.2f(3,a)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"a+0.2\\times\\frac{6-a}{3a} =4.450\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3a^2+1.2-0.2a =13.35a\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3a^2-13.55a+1.2 =0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"a =0.09036897\\ldots\\quad\\text{or}\\quad a=4.426298678\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\text{But }a&gt;2\\text{, so }a =4.426\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>The function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfies the differential equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\sqrt{2x+y^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the condition <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(1)=0.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. After one iteration of Euler's formula, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_{n+1}=y_n+\\dfrac1k f(x_n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, for integer <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, it is found that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_1=1.1250\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, which was correct to four decimal places.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac1k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Use your value for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac1k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to calculate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x_2,y_2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol><p><strong>Prerequisite Knowledge for Q15: First Order Linear Differential Equations</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =1,\\quad y_0=0.8\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =y_0+\\frac1k f(x_0,y_0)=0.8+\\frac1k f(1,0.8)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =0.8+\\frac1k\\sqrt{1.6+1}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"0.8+\\frac1k\\sqrt{2.64} =1.1250\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac1k =\\frac{1.1250-0.8}{\\sqrt{2.64}}=0.2000236728\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore \\text{Since }k\\text{ is an integer, }\\frac1k =\\frac15\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =0.8+\\frac1k f(1,0.8)=0.8+0.2\\sqrt{2.64}=1.124961536\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =1+0.2=1.2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_1+\\frac1k f(x_1,y_1)=1.124961536\\ldots+0.2f(1.2,1.124961536\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1.124961536\\ldots+0.2\\times1.914559599\\ldots=1.507873456\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =1.2+0.2=1.4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore (x_2,y_2) =(1.4,1.508)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfies <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=x+y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(0)=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Explain geometrically what the Euler formula <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_{n+1}=y_n+h(x_n+y_n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> represents.</p></li><li><p>Use Euler's method with step size <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to approximate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the exact value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>On a sketch, show the curve for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the tangent at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the first Euler step.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>At each point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x_n,y_n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the derivative <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=x_n+y_n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives the gradient of the tangent line. The formula moves <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units horizontally and then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\\times\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gradient vertically to obtain the next point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x_{n+1},y_{n+1})\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, which is the end of a straight-line segment tangent to the curve at the previous point.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =0,\\quad y_0=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =y_0+hf(x_0,y_0)=1+0.5f(0,1)=1+0.5\\times1=1.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =0+0.5=0.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_1+hf(x_1,y_1)=1.5+0.5f(0.5,1.5)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =0.5+0.5\\times2=2.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =0.5+0.5=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y =2.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}-y=x\\text{ has integrating factor }e^{\\int-1\\,dx}=e^{-x}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"e^{-x}\\frac{dy}{dx}-e^{-x}y =xe^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"ye^{-x} =\\int xe^{-x}\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"u =x,\\quad \\frac{dv}{dx}=e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{du}{dx} =1,\\quad v=-e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\int xe^{-x}\\,dx =-xe^{-x}+\\int e^{-x}\\,dx=-xe^{-x}-e^{-x}(+c)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"ye^{-x} =-xe^{-x}-e^{-x}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y =-x-1+ce^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y(0)=1:\\quad 1 =0-1+c\\quad\\therefore c=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y =2e^x-x-1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y(1) =2e-2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Sketch from the source worked-solutions PDF; it shows the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2e^x-x-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the tangent at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and the first Euler step to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0.5,1.5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.65/solutions/q15d-graph_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>A company monitors the total amount of data <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> GB uploaded to its servers during a live event. It is observed that the upload rate is directly proportional to the time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hours since the event began. After 4 hours, the upload rate is measured to be 24 GB per hour.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Determine the differential equation to model the total data uploaded.</p></li></ol><p>It is observed that one hour into the event, 1.5 GB has been uploaded.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>Use Euler's method with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.25\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to find the amount of data processed after 90 minutes, giving your answer to two decimal places.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Let the rate be <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dt}=kt\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"24=4k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dt}=6t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_0 =1,\\quad y_0=1.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =y_0+hf(t_0)=1.5+0.25f(1)=1.5+0.25\\times6=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_1 =1+0.25=1.25\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_1+hf(t_1)=3+0.25f(1.25)=3+0.25\\times7.5=4.875\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_2 =1.25+0.25=1.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y =4.88\\text{ GB (2 DP)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q17","number":17,"question":"<p>A post on a social media platform spreads as users share it. At time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hours since posting, the number of people who have seen the post is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The rate of change of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is affected by:</p><ul class=\"parts\"><li><p>sharing at a rate proportional to the current reach, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.08N\" data-display=\"false\"></span> people per hour</p></li><li><p>a reduction in visibility due to platform algorithms at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"500e^{-t}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> people per hour</p></li></ul><p>After 1 hour, the number of people who have seen the post is 4700. Use Euler's method with a step length of 0.5 to estimate the number of people who have seen the post after 2 hours have passed.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dN}{dt} =0.08N-500e^{-t}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_0 =1,\\quad N_0=4700\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"N_1 =N_0+hf(t_0,N_0)=4700+0.5f(1,4700)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =4700+0.5\\times192.060279414\\ldots=4796.030139707\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_1 =1+0.5=1.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"N_2 =N_1+hf(t_1,N_1)=4796.030139707\\ldots+0.5f(1.5,4796.030139707\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =4796.030139707\\ldots+0.5\\times272.117331102\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =4932.088805258\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_2 =1.5+0.5=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore N =4932\\text{ views}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.65-q18","number":18,"question":"<p>A leaking container is being monitored. The volume of water <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"W\" data-display=\"false\"></span> litres changes over time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hours due to three factors:</p><ul class=\"parts\"><li><p>Rainfall adds water at an average constant rate of 0.5 litres per hour.</p></li><li><p>Evaporation over each day removes water at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\sin^2\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}t\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> litres per hour.</p></li><li><p>Leakage removes water proportional to the current volume in the pond, at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.01W\" data-display=\"false\"></span> litres per hour.</p></li></ul><p>At the start of observation (at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>), the pond contains 100 litres of water. Use Euler's step by step method three times to estimate the amount of water in the container after 9 hours have passed. Give your answer to three significant figures.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dW}{dt} =0.5-2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}t\\right)-0.01W\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_0 =0,\\quad W_0=100\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"W_1 =W_0+hf(t_0,W_0)=1000+3f(0,1000)=1000+3\\times(-0.5)=98.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_1 =0+3=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"W_2 =W_1+hf(t_1,W_1)=98.5+3f(3,98.5)=98.5+3\\times(-1.485)=94.045\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_2 =3+3=6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"W_3 =W_2+hf(t_2,W_2)=94.045+3f(6,94.045)=94.045+3\\times(-2.44045)=86.72365\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_3 =3+6=9\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore W =86.7\\text{ litres (3 SF)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]}]